OL,3,GNEWSANon-league clubs tackle youth
OL,4,Aantisocial behaviour
OL,5,
OL,6,FNon-league football clubs across the
OL,7,FWest Midlands are working together to
OL,8,Ftry to tackle antisocial behaviour from
OL,9,Fteenagers causing trouble in and around
OL,10,Fgrounds.
OL,12,FRecent incidents include stones being
OL,13,Fthrown at away fans and an opposition
OL,14,Fteam's kit man being punched.
OL,16,FSome clubs are changing their ticket
OL,17,Frules so under-16s have to be
OL,18,Faccompanied by an adult, while others
OL,19,Fare in talks to come up with a
OL,20,Fcollaborative approach.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
